      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "There are genuine seductive textures \u2014 the amber light \u0027patient in a way that has nothing to do with patience,\u0027 the mass-and-gravity monologue, \u0027checking whether you are still yourself\u0027 \u2014 but they\u0027re immediately harnessed to exposition and plot-mechanics (Vig\u0027s contract logic, Quire\u0027s negotiation, the wipe-clause countdown), so the strange-beautiful keeps getting interrupted before it can fully pull the reader in.",
      "Fix": "Let at least one more beat linger purely in sensory/atmospheric wrongness (the cold, the dust, the amber pulse) before cutting to the next procedural complication, so allure has room to breathe rather than being immediately metabolized into plot."
    },
    {
      "Key": "open_grounded",
      "Title": "Open with the world doing its work",
      "Status": "fail",
      "Evidence": "The story opens directly with plot machinery: The Ledger\u0027s columns, a debt metaphor, then an urgent unclassified ping arriving mid-quote at a fabrication yard. The only \u0027world doing its work\u0027 beat is a single sentence about quoting cable pull rates before the inciting call interrupts it \u2014 there\u0027s no sustained grounded entry moment (commute, transaction, mundane observation) before the reader is asked to track relay routing, personhood-adjacent licensing, and a thirteen-year-old debt.",
      "Fix": "Open with an extended, unhurried beat of Ledger actually doing mundane work in Ashgrave (the quote, the yard, the city\u0027s indifferent rhythm) for a paragraph or two before the relay ping interrupts, so the reader falls into the world before the plot machinery of Renn\u0027s call and the dead process demands attention."
    },
    {
      "Key": "gloss_in_voice",
      "Title": "Gloss first mentions in-voice, never dump",
      "Status": "pass",
      "Evidence": "\u0027his neuretics \u2014 the neural mesh grown into his substrate \u2014\u0027 and \u0027the neuretic etching at the temples that reads Tier 3 to anyone who knows to look\u0027 both gloss the term in a single clause, folded into action beats rather than paused-on exposition; similarly \u0027Cinderfall Logistics leased that rack space, ran a distributed process across it, and pulled the Fleet\u0027s charter when the licensing math stopped adding up\u0027 delivers CorpoNation/charter backstory through Ledger\u0027s own accounting-brain train of thought rather than a lecture.",
      "Fix": null
    },
    {
