      "Evidence": "\u0027GLMZ\u0027 appears as a bare acronym on first use (\u0027the kind of gray, unglamorous infrastructure that runs half of GLMZ\u0027s cargo without anyone thinking about it once\u0027) with no expansion given before or after; similarly \u0027IP\u0027 (\u0027it\u0027s thirteen years dark and it\u0027s still holding an IP\u0027) is never glossed at all.",
      "Fix": "Add an in-voice expansion before each acronym\u0027s first use, e.g. introduce GLMZ as \u0027the Greater Loop Municipal Zone\u0027 and IP as \u0027an instance pointer\u0027 the first time each term appears."
    },
    {
      "Key": "human_crack",
      "Title": "Give the POV character one human crack",
      "Status": "warn",
      "Evidence": "The prose gestures at Ledger\u0027s interiority through the running audit-voice motif (\u0022the specific reluctance of a man asked to read his own autopsy report aloud,\u0022 the unfinished ledger entry for Renn), but there\u0027s no single unguarded flash where he\u0027s felt as a person rather than a function \u2014 even the closest candidate, his unspoken confession about the kill order and the park ranger testimony, stays filtered through analytical narration rather than landing as raw feeling.",
      "Fix": "Let one moment break the audit-register entirely \u2014 a physical tell, a memory fragment, or a line of dialogue to Renn or Green where Ledger\u0027s own grief surfaces unmediated by ledger-metaphor before he re-arms himself with the accounting language."
